In article <5329@ur-cc.UUCP> ars3_cif@uhura.cc.rochester.edu 
(Aaron Sher) writes:
>Does anyone know exactly what those damn colors on the ring of warning
>mean?  I played for like two or three years and I could never find a 
>pattern.
>
  You receive a warning when there is a monster in the vicinity whose
experience level is higher than your own; the color of the glow tells
you how much higher.  The colors, in order of increasing danger, are:
"white", "pink", "red", "ruby", "purple", and, worst of all,
"black".
  I can't think of any way to discover this except by experimenting a
lot with a stethoscope or, um, looking at the source.

